@@ -4,6 +4,18 @@
 
 Amounts are integer cents. `toCents("12.50")` returns `1250`, and `formatAmount(1250)` returns `"12.50"`.
 
+## Tax and discounts
+
+`computeInvoice(lines, { taxRatePercent, discountPercent = 0 })` in `src/tax.js` prices an invoice exactly, in integer cents.
+
+- Each line's net is `quantity × unitCents`; a negative quantity is a credit line.
+- The invoice discount is `discountPercent` of the sum of the positive line nets, rounded half to even.
+- The discount is split across positive lines in proportion to their nets using the largest-remainder method (ties go to the earlier line). Credit lines get no discount.
+- Each line's tax is `taxRatePercent` of its net minus its discount, rounded half to even (symmetric for negatives, so -13.5 becomes -14).
+- Rates must be between 0 and 100 with at most two decimal places.
+
+It returns `{ lines, netCents, discountCents, taxCents, grossCents }`, where each line has the same four fields and the totals are sums over the lines.
+
 ## Shipping
 
 Rates depend on the destination zone and the parcel weight.
